  "title": "web-edit 0.1a0",
  "summary": "Release: web-edit 0.1a0 I was working on a project from my phone using Codex Remote when I found myself wanting to edit a credentials file without round-tripping those credentials through the LLM itself. So... I had Codex and GPT-6 Astra Extra High build this Python web app which provides a web UI for viewing and editing files in a folder. It's intended to…",
  "content": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/web-edit/releases/tag/0.1a0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">web-edit 0.1a0</a></p>\n        <p>I was working on a project from my phone using Codex Remote when I found myself wanting to edit a credentials file without round-tripping those credentials through the LLM itself.</p>\n<p>So... I had Codex and GPT-6 Astra Extra High build this Python web app which provides a web UI for viewing and editing files in a folder. It&#x27;s intended to be run over Tailscale, so I can have an agent start this running and then edit files via my Tailscale network directly from my phone.</p>\n<p>Here&#x27;s the interface for browsing files in a folder:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot of a web file manager interface. Header reads &quot;WORKSPACE&quot; above the title &quot;Files&quot;, with buttons &quot;Refresh&quot;, &quot;Upload files&quot; and &quot;New file&quot; (dark green). A breadcrumb shows &quot;web-edit / web_edit / static&quot;. A table with columns &quot;Name&quot;, &quot;Size&quot;, &quot;Modified&quot; lists four files, each with &quot;Download ↓&quot; and &quot;Delete&quot; links: &quot;app.css&quot; 8.4 KB Oct 12, 2026; &quot;app.js&quot; 671.5 KB Oct 12, 2026; &quot;index.html&quot; 4.3 KB Oct 12, 2026 (underlined, as if hovered); &quot;THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt&quot; 32.3 KB Oct 12, 2026. Below the table: &quot;Images under 2 MB appear inline. Select a text file to edit it.&quot; A panel below is labelled &quot;UPLOAD QUEUE&quot; with heading &quot;Add files&quot; and a &quot;Close&quot; button. It has a &quot;Destination folder&quot; text field containing &quot;web_edit&quot;, then a dashed drop zone reading &quot;Choose files or drop them here&quot; and &quot;Set a path and filename for each file before uploading.&quot; with a &quot;Choose Files&quot; button and the text &quot;no files selected&quot;. A greyed-out &quot;Upload files&quot; button sits at the bottom right.\" src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/web-edit.webp\"></p>\n<p>Editing uses <a href=\"https://codemirror.net\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CodeMirror 6</a> - I was going to use <a href=\"https://microsoft.github.io/monaco-editor/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Monaco</a> but that still doesn&#x27;t have a great mobile experience yet.</p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/projects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">projects</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">python</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/ai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/tailscale\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">tailscale</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/generative-ai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">generative-ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llms\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">codex</a></p>",
